# P1239 — template for the critical-credential registry.
#
# The real list is NOT in this repo. It names which credentials are worth
# stealing, which is a target list, so it lives in the gitignored private half:
#
#     .private/docs/keyring-critical.txt
#
# Copy this file there and replace the categories below with the actual
# environment-variable names for your deployment, one per line. Comments and
# blank lines are ignored. Values never appear in either file — only names.
#
# The test for inclusion is "would losing this be unrecoverable or expensive?",
# not "is it a secret". Most credentials should stay in the plaintext half:
# friction spent on low-value keys is what gets the whole scheme switched off.

# <the production database master key>
# <the direct database connection string>
# <the operations mailbox password>
# <the transactional mail-sending key>
# <the blog admin key>
# <the social-publishing tokens>
# <the platform management token>
# <the source-control access token>
# <the hosting / FTP password>
# <the payments key>
